---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base lang="en" titulo="Fundación Entre Líneas" descripcion="Fundación Entre Líneas, founded in 1994, and its free monthly bulletin Leer Entre Líneas.">
  <section class="seccion">
    <div class="lectura">
      <p class="etiqueta">Since 1994</p>
      <h1>Fundación Entre Líneas</h1>
      <p class="intro"><em>Great lines for a better Venezuela</em></p>
      <hr class="linea" />
      <p>
        In 1994 María Denisse founded, together with her husband Luis Felipe Capriles, the
        <a href="https://venezuelaentrelineas.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fundación Entre Líneas</a>. Its work:
        producing printed educational material for Venezuelans, grounded in human and Christian values, for families,
        educators and young people.
      </p>

      <h2>The bulletin <em>Leer Entre Líneas</em></h2>
      <p>
        For years the foundation published the monthly bulletin
        <a href="https://venezuelaentrelineas.com/leer-entrelineas/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Leer Entre Líneas</em></a>,
        with more than 150 issues. It was distributed free of charge in almost every state of the country, until the paper
        shortage forced it to stop. María Denisse was its director and producer.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        “<span lang="es">Leer Entre Líneas</span> is a splendid monthly publication which, with great quality of design and
        printing, in a fresh and lively way promotes values, offers inspiration and is a constant spur to excellence. It is
        devoted to communicating great human and Christian values for a better life in society, to building a better
        Venezuela and to promoting the common good and social harmony, especially by showing the way for families, educators
        and young people.”
        <cite>Cardinal Jorge Urosa Savino</cite>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Recognition</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Monseñor Pellín Award (2005).</li>
        <li>Nominated for the Excellence Award of the organization Venezuela Competitiva.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The gathering “Builders of the New Participatory Venezuela”</h2>
      <p>
        In 2004 the foundation organized this gathering in Caracas with nearly a hundred volunteers. More than 40
        organizations and 600 people of every social, political, cultural and religious background attended, with coverage
        from more than 40 national and international media outlets. The aim: to sow hope and reconciliation among Venezuelans.
      </p>
      <p class="enlaces">
        <a class="boton" href="https://venezuelaentrelineas.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit Venezuela Entre Líneas</a>
        <a class="boton secundario" href="https://venezuelaentrelineas.com/leer-entrelineas/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the Leer Entre Líneas bulletin</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .enlaces { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 36px; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; margin-top: 1.6em; }
  blockquote { margin: 24px 0; padding: 20px 24px; background: var(--blanco); border-left: 3px solid var(--oro); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.1rem; font-style: italic; }
  cite { display: block; margin-top: 12px; font-style: normal; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: .9rem; color: var(--gris); }
</style>
